## 2. Helios-n facts (cite, do not invent)

From Helios arXiv:2406.08491:

- Without multiplexing: VCU129 fits ≈ d≤21 phenom / d≤17 circuit (LUT-bound).
- Helios-n: partition decoding graph into *n* sub-graphs; time-multiplex onto a physical **lattice**.
- Context switch at PE: store/load PE state in **local LUTRAM** (not BRAM — shallower depth) ≈ **1 clock cycle**.
- Cross-cut adjacent virtual PEs map to the **same** physical PE so boundary neighbor state stays in that PE’s local memory (avoids Heer-style extra lattice wires).
- Examples: d=27 Helios-4…27; d=51 Helios-51 (~544 ns/round reported).

Aether delta: state fields follow Aether H1–H5 (union-by-size, active = odd ∧ ¬boundary), not Helios min-cid / raw `codd`.

